								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/avatars/macross.gif" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								My Avatar can beat up your avatar!<br />
								<br />
								
								<a href="http://members.msn.com/kinladar@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/msntalk.gif" alt="kinladar@hotmail.com" border="0" /></a>
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=1"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org" title="http://www.rodcetnife.org" target="_blank"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/www_sm.gif" alt="WWW" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="mailto:truman@thewavz.com"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/email_sm.gif" alt="Email" title="Email" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1146.msg11320#msg11320"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1146.msg11320#msg11320">Re: EQ the Game - and how history played out</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #6 on:</b> September 20, 2004, 03:34:06 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							It does to a degree when you consider that I think alot of what made the current guild structures dates back to Luclin, and led into PoP. The guilds that held VT for the longest time, and owned that zone, were able to capitlize on that, and move quickly through PoP. <br /><br />Skill does play a part, organizing as well.<br /><br />Oh and Del, we knew you had access, that was why alot of what we did was never on the boards. <br /><br />But as you state yourself, it was as much keeping the other guilds in line, and out of the content that allowed Ascent to take, and hold the position they had for so long.<br /><br />It was only a matter of time before instanced content equalized things some. I expect Conviction to also benefit from this.<br /><br />As far as getting a guild geared efficiently, and such, it certainly does. But alot depends on what the guild&#039;s goals are. If Fires was totally and only focused on beating EiE/DA and Ascent to the top, I&#039;d cut the under 25% raid attendance people we have. Different ideals at work there.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
