	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg11323"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg2">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=174" title="View the profile of Delheru">Delheru</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Guild Leader<br />
								Splitpaw Gnoll<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 97<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/avatars/blank.gif" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=174"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1146.msg11323#msg11323"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1146.msg11323#msg11323">Re: EQ the Game - and how history played out</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #9 on:</b> September 20, 2004, 03:46:53 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							Well I have the info from your people that joined Ascent as well. Frankly Conviction seemed to have a more analytical approach to the game at most times, and some people who had very good knowledge of the game. This is different from being good players obviously. Many good players don&#039;t understand the game that well.<br /><br /><br />Once the game started getting trivialized (Luclin was the first one that moved from &quot;this zones OWNS your ass&quot; to &quot;entering this zone will be a pain in the ass&quot;), the differences between guilds were obviously going to go down, and focus more on time spent than anything else. The differences survived luclin mostly because of the cockblock that the Emperor so neatly allowed.<br /><br />The easier the game is, the smaller the differences will be, especially with instances and pretty much the whole server population being &quot;high end&quot; gamers of one sort or another. Of course instancing also increases the flow of loot in to the game massively, and as such forces the use of miscellaneous cockblock methods, which is in my opinion extremely stupid... competition created an extremely succesful cockblock, that most people didn&#039;t really blame on the game. Without the competition the community also suffers, which is equally lame. Oh well.<br /><br />However I suspect the order would be pretty similar with or without instances. I don&#039;t know how the current Ascent would place, as the leadership has not been truly tested yet, but with the old bunch we&#039;d be at the top, DA/EiE would be second... this is where I perceive a potential difference: Conviction might be third.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
