							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1146.msg11326#msg11326"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1146.msg11326#msg11326">Re: EQ the Game - and how history played out</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #11 on:</b> September 20, 2004, 04:31:23 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							I would have quit sooner if there was instancing from the start, unless they would have kept raids short. But instancing really killed the game for me over time, it took away racing and the hard work of getting to a target fast and getting it done before anyone else, the hard work to do it first before anyone else, with instancing im not going to raid a stupid 8 hour raid that anyone can do to be like everyone else, i want to be one of the only ones there to show for the hard work.<br /><br /> I want it hard or i want it easy, not this middle crap eq is now, in wow its instaced and thats fiine, cause 1 its not as time consoming as EQ&nbsp; was so far and we will see more soon when raids get added to beta, and loot is pretty plentyfull, and the game is FUN to play, so basicly i want it fun and plentyfull, or hard and rare, not this middle of the road long as raid with crappy rewards anyone that wasnt to clear tons of boring yard trash that anyone can do in there own instance.<br /><br />PS ignore the Demottesse
						</td>
					</tr>
